# Build output from the demo sources a chapter ships so its figures can be
# checked. Following the build line in optimizer-demo.rs drops a .s file next
# to it, and that should not show up as untracked work. This file is repository
# tooling configuration and keeps the Tock license, as learning/.lcignore does.
*.s

# Except one that is a source rather than build output. Chapter 6 ships the
# assembly its figures quote, and check.py assembles it on every run, so a
# clone without this file would run the gate green with the check silently
# skipped and the page citing a file that is not there. Which is what happened:
# the rule above was written for chapter 1's build artefact and swallowed
# chapter 6's source the first time it was committed.
!ch06-asking-the-kernel/syscall-demo.s
